[
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Manoeuvring Models  (Module 4)",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Prepared together with Andrew Ross",
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Dr Tristan Perez",
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Centre for Complex Dynamic Systems and Control (CDSC)",
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Professor Thor I Fossen",
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Department of Engineering Cybernetics",
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/8962ba0bc872ad077847583e2841494ce51a6476cb145d28b6251702cc8e12a0.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/e29b613ed08a3f4363bdbd18f84ff9baef4b407f0950166ce6b405c5c0a30cbe.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "1",
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Vectorial Representation for Ships",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "From robotics to ship modeling (Fossen 1991)",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "It is here assumed that the hydrodynamic coefficients are <u>frequency independent.</u>",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This will be relaxed later!",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Consider the classical robot manipulator model:",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "\\- **q** is a vector of joint angles",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "\\-     is a vector of torque",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "\\- **M** and **C** are the system inertia and Coriolis matrices",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This model structure can be used as foundation to write the 6 DOF marine vessel equations of motion in a compact <em>vectorial</em> setting (<strong>Fossen 1994, 2002</strong>):",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "\\- body velocities:",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "\\- position and Euler angles:",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- **M, C** and **D** denote the system inertia,    Coriolis and damping matrices",
            "- **g is a vector of gravitational and buoyancy**    **forces and moments**"
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/48fea1834a89ef3c00d3de04946fe2171616d0297d80559c63c3aa220a55d356.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/375547676fd0ff01ed8568b255d20c46389845ea3b127683bbfede0b2fc40b91.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "2",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Rigid-Body Equations of Motion",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/a6987b94b8d7d60990362601d447b2456e37823fdba7825363bc8579bf93f798.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Newtonian Formulation (Body Frame)",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "where",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<em><strong>M</strong>RB</em> rigid-body system inertia matrix",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<em><strong>C</strong>RB</em>  rigid-body Coriolis/centripetal matrix",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "*Rigid-body system inertia matrix*",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<em>See</em> <em><strong>Fossen (1994, 2002</strong>) for parameterizations of</em> <em><strong>C</strong>RB</em>",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The generalized forces on a floating vessel are <u>superpositioned</u>:",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Hydrodynamic radiation-induced forces + viscous damping",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "3",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Radiation-Induced Hydrodyn. Forces",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Forces on the body when the body is forced to oscillate with the wave excitation frequency and there are <u>no incident waves</u> (Faltinsen 1990):",
            "    1. *Added mass* due to the inertia of the surrounding fluid",
            "    2. Radiation-induced (linear) *potential damping* due to the energy carried away by generated surface waves",
            "    3. Restoring forces due to *Archimedes* (weight and buoyancy)"
        ],
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<strong>Faltinsen (1990).</strong> <em>Sea Loads on Ships and Offshore Structures</em>, Cambridge.",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "“hydrodynamic mass-damper-spring”",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "4",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Added Mass and Inertia",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/ddec99524292799410562b7651887c57732bc723c4b09d6a2386f219b369d11b.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Fluid Kinetic Energy",
            "- The concept of fluid kinetic energy:",
            "- can be used to derive the added mass terms.",
            "- Any motion of the vessel will induce a motion in the otherwise stationary fluid. In order to allow the vessel to pass through the fluid, it must move aside and then close behind the vessel.",
            "- Consequently, the fluid motion possesses kinetic energy that it would lack otherwise (**Lamb 1932**)."
        ],
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "5",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "6 DOF Body-Fixed Representation for Added Mass  (Includes Coriolis/Centripetal Terms due to Added Mass)",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/fe5edd48c16864c15bf03657441bec50309f8fbec9d69779d768c7e87674fd88.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**Kirchhoff's Equations (1869)**",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "kinetic energy due",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "to the fluid",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/23aa4e2096c95f900320caa1a583f1c2a42be99f1f5eb93f99afb6cdc417ea27.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "***CA(n)***",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "***MA***",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "6",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Viscous Hydrodynamic Damping",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- In addition to potential damping we have to include other <u>dissipative viscous terms</u> like <em>skin friction, wave drift damping etc</em>:"
        ],
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Total *hydrodynamic* *damping matrix*:"
        ],
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- The hydrodynamic forces and moments       can be now be written as the sum of                 :"
        ],
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/5299b380797de2e38067d694178aeb935d9b4a6607b4d9eb088bf9033d7b15d3.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "7",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Equations of Motion",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The resulting model is (frequency-independent coefficients):",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/65007c983de27876f8293d2abe4c3121f8fde1bd299e2684d95a9b7c59c4445d.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/f20ee8f59ee386dd66951c4830e8be655e924ff52f07c05506e36c24f94e0e43.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "*System inertia matrix including added mass*",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Linear mass-damper-spring",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(frequency-independent)",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "8",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Manoeuvring Hydrodynamics",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "In <u>classical manoeuvring theory</u>, the forces are modelled at a general non-linear function:",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "A particular affine parameterization is then used, and the coefficients are estimated linear regression from the data.",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The disadvantage of this model representation to a energy-based (Lagrangian) approach is that model reduction, symmetry/skew-symmetry properties, positive matrices, etc.  are difficult to exploit in simulation and control design.",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This model can, however, be related to the <u>Lagrangian model</u>: as shown by Ross et al. 2007:",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "9",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Parameterisations",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Two types of parameterisations for the hydrodynamic forces are generally used in classical manoeuvring theory:",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Truncated Taylor-series expansions:",
            "    - Davison and Shiff (1946): 1st-order (linear) terms.",
            "    - Abkowitz (1964): odd terms up to 3rd  order."
        ],
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- 2nd -order modulus",
            "    - Fedyaevsky and Sobolev (1963)",
            "    - Norrbin (1970)"
        ],
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "10",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Parameterisations",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- 2nd -order modulus"
        ],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Taylor-series"
        ],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/7a5d402ca911efd4501750db78570273a2c67dd883f129bd8e3484292f1d4e6e.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/fcc54bf569d57da36fe2b710a67b89f0b13c4cd852196dc94ce4469d192a0913.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "11",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Parameterisations",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "As commented by *Clarke (2003),*",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Taylor expansions give rise to a smooth representation of the forces, but have no physical meaning."
        ],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- 2nd-order modulus expansions represent well the hydrodynamic forces at angles of incidence: <u>cross-flow drag</u>."
        ],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "12",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Taylor-Series Expansions",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Where the partial derivatives are taken at an equilibrium:",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "13",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Model of Abkowitz (1964)",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/7c554036bec048d92472ada092e1af6cbdff031ccd51a8b01d636c47997000aa.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The coefficients are called hydrodynamic derivatives.",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Many terms are set to zero by exploiting physically properties. If not, there will thousands of coefficients.",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "14",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Model of Norrbin (1970)",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/8b5584736a385803dbe01c1abc211764ad74959dcb014963ce0259e0b7f3268b.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "15",
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "2nd-Order Modulus",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "From Blanke and Christiansen (1986):",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/be2163bfe56b5768fe4a5566a3edf724d1da128f3fa9b5868a11dd03851033b9.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "16",
        "page_idx": 15
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Measurement of Hydrodynamic Derivatives",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "PMM",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Experiments with model tests.",
            "- Full scale sea trials and system identification.",
            "- Theoretical prediction methods.",
            "- Regression analysis results from similar designs."
        ],
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Model tests that can be performed",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Straight line in a towing tank,",
            "- Rotating arm,",
            "- Planar motion mechanism PMM,",
            "- Oscillator tests,",
            "- Free running (radio controlled)."
        ],
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/1f3d48bc41896fbfe654affbd377c431aa6343eae1d22889ec0ba5e636a26492.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/c36f79d29b43da48dc3bba1ae5cae85c4a320433816c3aa8f61608e55a6e7a14.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "17",
        "page_idx": 16
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Experimental Methods",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "***Model testing in Peerlesspool in London***",
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "18",
        "page_idx": 17
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Measurement of Hydrodynamic Derivatives",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/2a540eed895eb60e5116e33c9192556290f830df44c078c1494a7c3245214369.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Rotating arm",
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "19",
        "page_idx": 18
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Typical Tests",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/640d95e7c1de9d908ec4bb3515e630b888457b7f36e0beb976ae3f0bc4c94750.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Pure Sway:",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Pure yaw:",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Drift and yaw:",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Different tests are used to fit different parts of the model.",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/093f78a36ebd3d1a6f594a784acfb3f410a20dcc179c1795d2b06f15118d9366.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/6b897eab7e60e10c81fb806daed4e794754d078a768bdb760ba36b743e116258.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "20",
        "page_idx": 19
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Measurement of Hydrodynamic Derivatives",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "During the model tests, the model is forces to move and forces velocities and accelerations are recorded.",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Then the hydrodynamic derivatives are estimated from regression analysis.",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/8f19b17499289a9c24d513a2fdfc61bb550a0b4599a2ad3b8cb3671008227cdb.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "21",
        "page_idx": 20
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "A Novel 4 DOF Manoeuvring Model",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Ross et. al. (2007)  has reassessed the manoeuvring models in the literature, and formulated a novel 4 DOF (surge, sway, roll, yaw) <u>Lagrangian model</u> using first principles and superposition of:",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Potential (added mass)",
            "- Circulation effects: lift and drag",
            "- Effect of roll on circulation effects",
            "- Cross-flow drag."
        ],
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The advantage of the Lagrangian model is its vector representation which is tailor made for <u>energy-based control design (Lyapunov)</u>.",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/2781b4720365103c9164e4d429e6beb224b09cf84dc85de5b9767c692daa7532.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "22",
        "page_idx": 21
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Added Mass and Coriollis",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The 4 DOF solution of Kirchhoff’s equations can be expressed as (Fossen, 2002)",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/ff2c39c2903f75d348db1ce724087b8316130b0e7df24817655815f3c96ccf76.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Added mass",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Added mass Coriollis and Centripetal terms",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/703c3b2327a2dc6c9841f35c1ae1ca29d0a286c2cf33fc5ca1e92f8a14d2f820.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "23",
        "page_idx": 22
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Model of Ross et al. (2007)",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Circulation effects (lift and drag), effect of roll on circulation effects and cross-flow drag (modulus representation) are derived in Ross et al. (2007):",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "where the components are:",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/5a406a4d1195ae67e8da7c78bd70f61a8f6ab59c7e98269a4c7df6c6c9f83b23.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "24",
        "page_idx": 23
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Manoeuvring Model",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 24
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Combining all the terms in a matrix  for, we obtain the manoeuvring equations in Lagrangian form (Fossen 1994, 2002).",
        "page_idx": 24
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/2781b4720365103c9164e4d429e6beb224b09cf84dc85de5b9767c692daa7532.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 24
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 24
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 24
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "25",
        "page_idx": 24
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Model Validation with PMM Data",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 25
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "To validate the model, Ross et al. (2007) used data of several PMM tests, and perform a regression based on the model structure derived.",
        "page_idx": 25
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Then compared the fit with that of a model fitted by a tank testing facility to the same dataset.",
        "page_idx": 25
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 25
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 25
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "26",
        "page_idx": 25
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Fitting Using PMM Data @ 30kt",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 26
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/725d97fcc5cda614de0d090a11aa289c819da83f60c9abb5fe21ab8d993d2501.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 26
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 26
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 26
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "27",
        "page_idx": 26
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Validation in Full Scale (Perez et al.,2007)",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 27
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Perez et al. (2007) fitted a simplified model to data recorded on full scale manoeuvres of Austal’s Trimaran Hull 260.",
        "page_idx": 27
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/baec1babc4e209fd51f08aadbe6330b248b8de34aec293dc7ece65af30777d5c.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 27
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The parameters were fitted with data of a 20-20 zig-zag test, and then the model validated with data of a 10-10 zig-zag test.",
        "page_idx": 27
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 27
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 27
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "28",
        "page_idx": 27
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Simplified Model",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 28
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The model was simplified according to the that of Blanke (1981). This was done because the excitation signal was not rich enough to estimate all the parameters—the zig-zag test is not designed for system identification!",
        "page_idx": 28
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/a09378a2d9997adedad82491323ae7c5c34cce02f690f38e6ddff0afd3a02ca7.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 28
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/8522382e6e3ef9dc6a000ab0a796f0bd88337dff25abaa5e929c26164e27d8fe.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 28
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/9a1a28321278b6d56110a001375dcc18812f8962f2f62a39f5af2e8e65349857.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 28
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 28
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 28
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "29",
        "page_idx": 28
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Model Fitting (20-20 ZZ)",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 29
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/baec1babc4e209fd51f08aadbe6330b248b8de34aec293dc7ece65af30777d5c.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 29
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 29
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 29
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "30",
        "page_idx": 29
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Model Validation (10-10 ZZ)",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 30
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/baec1babc4e209fd51f08aadbe6330b248b8de34aec293dc7ece65af30777d5c.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 30
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/fefda89748f4986584a3fcc7097c2f25c393741ea92464dd520eee8a9e6c56bf.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 30
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 30
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 30
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "31",
        "page_idx": 30
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Effects of Currents",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 31
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "In some applications, where positioning is important, the effects of current must be considered:",
        "page_idx": 31
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The current has to effects, which are represented with the velocity of the vessel relative to the current velocity:",
        "page_idx": 31
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Potential: The Munk moment is incorporated in the added mass Coriollis-Centripetal terms.",
            "- Viscous: eddy making and skin friction. These are incorporated in the cross-flow drag."
        ],
        "page_idx": 31
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "03/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 31
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 31
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "32",
        "page_idx": 31
    },
